// src/sema/sema.zen
// Semantic analysis: the middle of the compiler.
//
// This file is the module's public surface and nothing else — a folder
// root is a file of starred re-exports, which is what makes a folder
// work. A name absent from this list is module-private on purpose.
//
// THE SHAPE, in four sentences, so nobody has to read five files to
// start:
//
//   - Sema is MEMOIZED QUERIES, not passes. `alloc.Checker(tree)` builds
//     the engine; `type_of(id, ctx)` and `type_from_ast(id, ctx)` are
//     the two that answer about a node, and both cache on the node's id.
//     That is what `ast_id.zen` made ids `Eq + Hash` for.
//   - A TYPE IS AN INTERNED ID. `TyId` compares by equality because the
//     store canonicalises: `A | B` and `B | A` are one id, and that is
//     what makes an error set a set rather than a tree walk.
//   - A DIAGNOSTIC IS A VALUE. Nothing raises. The only `Err` anywhere
//     in this folder is `AllocError`, so a program full of mistakes
//     still analyses and yields every diagnostic it owes.
//   - NAMES RESOLVE THROUGH THE MODULE GRAPH, and `*` gates every hop.
//     Re-export is an import whose bindings are starred, so following an
//     import and filtering by `exported` is the whole of the export
//     rule — there is no second mechanism.
//
// WHAT IS NOT HERE YET is listed in the report that came with this
// folder rather than hidden behind an optimistic export: overload
// resolution, impl-supplied members, exhaustiveness and the
// provable-trap rule are named in `sema_diag.zen`'s fault set and are
// not yet raised by a check.

// how a declaration and a member are named, so a memo can key on one
DeclId*, MemberId*, ImplId*, owner*, member_at* = sema.sema_id

// what sema computes: the interned type language
TyId*, Ty*, Types*                       = sema.sema_ty
Prim*, TyNamed*, TyFn*, TyUnion*, TyVar* = sema.sema_ty
ResForm*, TyRes*, key_before*            = sema.sema_ty

// what sema says when a program means nothing
SemaFault*, Diag*, message*, render*     = sema.sema_diag
NameFault*, TypeFault*, PairFault*       = sema.sema_diag
write_pos*, write_usize*                 = sema.sema_diag

// what a name means, and who is allowed to ask
DefKind*, Def*, ImportBinding*           = sema.sema_def
ModuleTable*, World*, dotted*, decl_at*  = sema.sema_def

// THE ENGINE
Checker*, Ctx*, Binding*                 = sema.sema_check
is_prim*, is_integer*, is_float*         = sema.sema_check
